{"type":"text","timestamp":1794582867284,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d0ffecbTUB800qIwYAx","part":{"id":"prt_1d57954ee001Q3UL56R6ectfCT","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d0ffecbTUB800qIwYAx","messageID":"msg_1d579446c001RpVCZ7CbtDWpjP","type":"text","text":"T010 is done. Only the corpus file changed, all five verify checks match the task's expected output, and the checkbox was left unticked.\n\nFiles written:\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (four rows: `cmd-create-skill-typed-01` and `sv-07` got the prompt and `expected_command` rewrite, `cmd-create-skill-plain-tune-01` got `expected_command` only, the holdout row got `expected_command` only via the exact `sed` substitution).\n\nVerify output, run from the repository root:\n\n```\n$ awk '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ && /\"expected_command\":\"\\/create:sk-skill\"/ {n++} END {print n+0}' $CORPUS\n1\n\n$ rg -c '\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"' $CORPUS\n(no output, exit 1)\n\n$ jq -c 'select(.expected_command == \"/create:sk-skill\") | [.split, .row_type]' $CORPUS | sort | uniq -c\n   1 [\"holdout\",\"plain\"]\n   1 [\"none\",\"slash-variant\"]\n   1 [\"none\",\"typed\"]\n   1 [\"tune\",\"plain\"]\n\n$ jq -c . $CORPUS > /dev/null\n(all 176 lines parse, exit 0)\n\n$ git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --numstat HEAD -- $CORPUS\n4\t4\t.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl\n```\n\nThe four pairs match `spec.md` section 2 exactly. Before editing I confirmed the three non-holdout splits (`none`, `tune`, `none`) by id, and the holdout row was never read or printed: only the count was reported.\n\nNothing was left undone. No other file was touched and no git state was changed.","time":{"start":1794582861038,"end":1794582867284}}}
